--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bounded-authored-compiler.md
@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@
+# Bounded authored package compiler
+
+## Status and dependency order
+
+This is a source-only M5 increment. No configuration, build, authored compiler
+execution or generated-artifact execution has validated this candidate. It does
+not complete M5 and is not stage one, stage two or a self-hosting result.
+
+The source depends on the retained raw-syntax ABI and binary handoff in PR445,
+then the snapshot-to-reader composition in PR446, and the scalar lowering
+component in PR447. Those components require their own exact-tree runtime and
+linked-boundary checks before this compiler receives first-run admission. The
+driver does not extend any existing selector's caps, corpus or aggregate
+membership. Its separate selector requires independent complete-workload
+admission under the unchanged production supervisor.
+
+## Entry and complete input
+
+`tools/compiler/bounded_compiler` is an ordinary three-file Chibi package. Its
+entry is `Compile(project: string, paths: string[], sources: string[],
+abi: scalar_lowering.Target) -> Result`.
+
+The caller supplies the complete explicit package source snapshot as owned
+strings. There is no disk discovery, imported-source callback or hidden native
+source preparation. Paths and sources have equal lengths, from one through
+three. Each source is at most 1,024 bytes; project and supplied paths are at most
+240 bytes. The existing snapshot validates routing, UTF-8, package headers and
+graph consistency. Each retained tree is at most 512 nodes; retained document
+keys and package identities are at most 240 bytes. An ingress that accepts raw
+bytes must reject embedded NUL before converting them to runtime strings.
+
+The accepted graph contains exactly one import-free package. Every file is
+walked before lowering; package-header/comment-only sibling files are accepted.
+Exactly one declaration may occur across the complete package: an explicitly
+`pure`, nongeneric, identifier-named, zero-argument function returning one
+ordinary `int` or `bool`. Its body contains exactly one ordinary return. Other
+declarations, extra statements and unhandled expressions reject. The driver
+does not compile only the selected function while silently dropping other
+source contents.
+
+## Supported expression subset
+
+- Boolean literals, parentheses, Boolean `!`/`not`, `&&`/`and`, `||`/`or`, and
+  equal/not-equal comparisons.
+- Exact decimal I32 literals in direct `int` return or explicit `cast<int>`
+  context, including signed minimum. Out-of-range, hexadecimal, fractional and
+  exponent literals reject in this increment.
+- Identity `cast<int>`, integer unary plus/minus/inversion, add/subtract/multiply,
+  bitwise and/or/xor, and ordinary scalar comparisons. Binary integer operands
+  must already have explicit `int` types, such as
+  `cast<int>(19) + cast<int>(23)`. Implicit numeric inference is unsupported;
+  even `19 + 23` rejects rather than inventing a second inference policy.
+- No variables, calls, numeric conversions, division, remainder, shifts,
+  aggregates, tasks, effects, ECS declarations or source imports.
+
+ReadExpression uses explicit frames, at most 64 visits and 24 lowered rows.
+There is no recursive expression traversal. It preserves source ranges and
+constructs the existing scalar lowering typed tables; it does not provide
+precomputed native semantic answers to Chibi. Existing signature_reader owns
+the accepted result annotation, lexical_binding owns declaration admission and
+stable identities, and scalar_lowering owns instruction/control-flow selection,
+including short circuit. Supported integer operations retain the existing
+width-wrapping runtime semantics.
+
+## Exact source-to-artifact path
+
+1. Chibi checks the request bounds and constructs source_snapshot inputs.
+2. `source_snapshot.Build` uses the existing raw Tree-sitter and JSON primitives
+   while Chibi owns paths, package extraction, routing, syntax diagnostics and
+   package graph decisions.
+3. `analysis_state.DocumentsForPackage` and `TreeForDocument` supply retained
+   reader trees. Chibi inspects every package member and rejects unsupported
+   declarations before encoding.
+4. Existing authored signature_reader and lexical_binding process the accepted
+   header. Chibi ReadExpression builds Bool/I32 typed rows from source nodes.
+5. `scalar_lowering.Lower` constructs the bounded instruction plan. Unsupported
+   target facts and invalid typed rows reject before the payload capability.
+6. The private producer primitive receives only that plan, authored IDs, entry
+   text and scalar result storage. The native scalar decoder replays it; existing
+   builder verification, optimization/finalization and prepared serialization
+   produce one inner CHIBIPRE version-14 module.
+7. Artifact.chibi constructs the complete one-module CHIBICLO version-1 envelope,
+   including magic, root/module identity, counts, lengths, name and payload. All
+   envelope words are authored little-endian encoding. The inner payload is
+   bounded to 65,536 bytes; the envelope is bounded to 65,832 bytes.
+8. `Result.Compiled` returns full-width module/entry IDs and owned bytes. A
+   fresh compiler_host API instance can validate/load those resulting bytes and
+   invoke the declared zero-argument function on bytecode or SLJIT.
+
+The module identity is the existing lexical `ID("module", package_identity)`;
+the function ID comes from the existing package-scope `binding.Declare` path.
+Results and diagnostics are ordinary owned invocation data.
+
+## Explicit native boundary and remaining work
+
+`compiler_prepared_scalar(plan, module, function, entry, result_storage)` is a
+private producer-only primitive. Its immutable service supplies the trusted
+scalar_lowering.Plan.Ready tag from bootstrap metadata. It never accepts source
+text, syntax trees, typed semantic IR, package preparation requests or an old
+compiler callback. It returns one inner prepared byte array and a diagnostic.
+The native core verifies zero arguments/state, one ordinary declared scalar
+result and the existing plan schema. It does not select opcodes or assemble
+the package envelope.
+
+The native finalizer, module publication and inner serializer remain declared
+transitional compiler dependencies. This increment authors the source frontend,
+lowering control and outer artifact policy; it does not claim that all compiler
+artifact construction has moved to Chibi.
+
+The existing runtime-only chibi-compiler-host is unchanged. Neither the new
+producer files nor frontend/writer dependencies are added to its link inputs or
+catalog. The compiler closure itself currently requires the private producer
+fixture and cannot run in that runtime-only host. Stage zero prepares the
+compiler implementation files only; the tests then pass user-source strings to
+the authored Compile entry. Only the generated user artifact is handed to the
+runtime-only host. A supported isolated producer product, complete compiler
+language coverage, authored inner encoding, bootstrap compatibility checks and
+stage-one/stage-two compilation of the complete compiler remain open work.
+
+No public command, language grammar, project schema, project version, installed
+SDK export or migration changes. No old compiler/recovery path is removed.
+
+## Required verification
+
+The separate C pico_unit suite must prepare only the declared compiler closure,
+check successful and rejected complete sources on both compiler backends,
+assert zero payload calls for source rejection, compare deterministic artifact
+bytes across backends and repeats, retire source/producer ownership, then load
+and run every accepted artifact through both target backends. These are fresh
+host API instances in the same test process; they do not establish a separate
+runtime-only executable-process result. It must also
+verify byte limits, precise signed literals, wrapped arithmetic, meaningful
+changed-source output, malformed native declarations and incompatible target
+facts. Counters report attempted work even on failure.
+
+Finite source counts, request/callback/parser bounds, output storage and target
+invocation counts belong to the exact candidate admission report. Build timing
+is separate from the single unchanged 60-second test deadline. Source-only
+review, formatting or admission does not establish an executed test result.
diff --git a/src/toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.c b/src/toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.c
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+#include "toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.h"
+
+#include "execution/definition.h"
+#include "execution/module_builder.h"
+#include "execution/prepared.h"
+#include "execution/scalar_lowering_plan.h"
+#include "support/array.h"
+#include "support/xalloc.h"
+
+#include <assert.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+static bool fail(char *error, size_t size, const char *message)
+{
+    if (size) {
+        snprintf(error, size, "%s", message);
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+static bool entry_valid(const char *entry)
+{
+    if (!entry || !entry[0]) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    for (int i = 1; i <= COMPILER_PREPARED_SCALAR_MAX_ENTRY; i++) {
+        if (!entry[i]) {
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+bool compiler_prepared_scalar_write(
+    const pin_value *value,
+    uint64_t ready_tag,
+    const compiler_prepared_scalar_declaration *declaration,
+    unsigned char **bytes,
+    size_t *length,
+    char *error,
+    size_t size
+)
+{
+    assert(bytes && length && error && size);
+    *bytes = NULL;
+    *length = 0;
+    if (size) {
+        error[0] = 0;
+    }
+    if (!value || !ready_tag || !declaration || !declaration->module ||
+        !declaration->function || !entry_valid(declaration->entry) ||
+        (declaration->result != PIN_BOOL && declaration->result != PIN_I32)) {
+        return fail(error, size, "invalid scalar callable declaration");
+    }
+    scalar_lowering_builder holder = { 0 };
+    if (!scalar_lowering_decode(value, ready_tag, &holder, error, size)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    const behavior_function *definition = behavior_function_builder_definition(
+        holder.builder
+    );
+    if (holder.variable_count || definition->argument_count ||
+        definition->variable_count || definition->result_count != 1 ||
+        definition->result_defaults[0].type != declaration->result ||
+        definition->result_defaults[0].container != PIN_CONTAINER_SINGLE ||
+        definition->result_kinds[0] != BEHAVIOR_VALUE) {
+        scalar_lowering_builder_free(&holder);
+        return fail(error, size, "scalar callable requires no arguments/state and one declared result");
+    }
+    behavior_function *body = scalar_lowering_finish(&holder, error, size);
+    scalar_lowering_builder_free(&holder);
+    if (!body) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    /* The authored evaluator already writes context.results and reaches
+     * BF_RETURN. Only its module role changes; no instruction is rewritten. */
+    execution_module_plan *plan = execution_module_plan_new();
+    plan->id = declaration->module;
+    plan->valid = true;
+    execution_module_function function = { .id = declaration->function,
+                                           .kind = EXECUTION_FUNCTION_AUTHORED,
+                                           .entry = xstrdup(declaration->entry),
+                                           .body = body };
+    apush(plan->functions, function);
+    plan->function_count = 1;
+    execution_module *module = execution_module_finish(&plan, BEHAVIOR_BYTECODE, error, size);
+    if (!module) {
+        execution_module_plan_free(plan);
+        return false;
+    }
+    bool written = execution_prepared_write(module, bytes, length, error, size);
+    execution_module_free(module);
+    if (!written) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (!*length || *length > COMPILER_PREPARED_SCALAR_MAX_BYTES) {
+        free(*bytes);
+        *bytes = NULL;
+        *length = 0;
+        return fail(error, size, "scalar prepared module exceeds bounded output storage");
+    }
+    return true;
+}
diff --git a/src/toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.h b/src/toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.h
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+#ifndef CHIBI_TOOLCHAIN_COMPILER_PREPARED_SCALAR_H
+#define CHIBI_TOOLCHAIN_COMPILER_PREPARED_SCALAR_H
+
+#include "types/value.h"
+
+enum
+{
+    COMPILER_PREPARED_SCALAR_MAX_ENTRY = 240,
+    COMPILER_PREPARED_SCALAR_MAX_BYTES = 64 * 1024
+};
+typedef struct
+{
+    uint64_t module, function;
+    const char *entry;
+    pin_type result;
+} compiler_prepared_scalar_declaration;
+
+/* Transitional, private PRODUCER dependency. Decodes an authored schema-1
+ * scalar_lowering.Plan with the unchanged scalar_lowering adapter, verifies
+ * exactly zero arguments/state and one ordinary Bool/I32 result, and wraps the
+ * body as one callable. ready_tag comes from trusted Plan export metadata.
+ * Identity and result declaration are authored choices; this bridge derives
+ * neither from source, names, packages, syntax or semantic records.
+ *
+ * Native builder verification/optimization/finalization and prepared writing
+ * remain explicit compiler dependencies. No target execution or backend JIT
+ * occurs here. The returned bytes are one INNER prepared module, never a
+ * CHIBICLO envelope. Success transfers malloc storage to the caller (free()).
+ * Failure clears bytes/length; inputs are borrowed only for this call.
+ * bytes, length and a nonempty error buffer are required.
+ * Do not link this producer into the runtime-only compiler_host. */
+bool compiler_prepared_scalar_write(
+    const pin_value *plan,
+    uint64_t ready_tag,
+    const compiler_prepared_scalar_declaration *,
+    unsigned char **bytes,
+    size_t *length,
+    char *error,
+    size_t error_size
+);
+
+#endif
diff --git a/test/language/bounded_compiler_chibi.c b/test/language/bounded_compiler_chibi.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/language/bounded_compiler_chibi.c
@@ -0,0 +1,773 @@
+#include "bounded_compiler_chibi.h"
+
+#include "backend.h"
+#include "bounded_compiler_chibi_source.h"
+#include "compiler_fixture.h"
+#include "compiler_prepared_fixture.h"
+#include "execution/definition.h"
+#include "execution/module.h"
+#include "execution/prepared.h"
+#include "execution/service.h"
+#include "execution/status.h"
+#include "support/array.h"
+#include "support/xalloc.h"
+#include "third_party/pico_headers/pico_unit.h"
+#include "toolchain/compiler_host.h"
+#include "toolchain/compiler_json.h"
+#include "toolchain/compiler_prepared_scalar.h"
+#include "toolchain/compiler_syntax.h"
+#include "types/array.h"
+#include "types/union.h"
+
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+/* SOURCE-ONLY, UNEXECUTED proposal. Bootstrap parses only the 18 shipped
+ * compiler/dependency files, never any CASE source below. The authored driver
+ * alone chooses semantic/lowering facts from each user source. Its private raw
+ * parser and prepared-payload callback are interposed only for work counting.
+ * One fixed corpus, two compiler backends, four compiler/target combinations;
+ * no timing loops, subprocesses, runtime files, network, rendering or GPU.
+ * First-run exact-source/resource admission and one production shared 60-second
+ * deadline are required. Context budgets reset in child activations and are
+ * not an aggregate instruction ceiling. See the source-only workload note. */
+enum
+{
+    ACCEPTED = 14,
+    REJECTED = 25,
+    CASES = ACCEPTED + REJECTED,
+    SOURCE_CAP = 1024,
+    PATH_CAP = 240,
+    ARTIFACT_CAP = 64 * 1024 + 56 + 240,
+    COMPILE_BUDGET = 3000000,
+    TARGET_BUDGET = 128
+};
+static const char PACKAGE[] = "project:bounded_compiler";
+static const char
+    VALID[] = "package facts\nAnswer :: pure fn()->int { return 42; }";
+typedef struct
+{
+    const char *name;
+    const char *project;
+    const char *paths[4];
+    const char *sources[4];
+    int path_count, source_count;
+    const char *expected;
+    bool wrong_abi;
+} request;
+static request cases[CASES];
+typedef struct
+{
+    unsigned char *bytes;
+    size_t length;
+    uint64_t module, entry;
+    int location[5];
+    char diagnostic[512];
+} saved;
+static saved outputs[2][CASES];
+static compiler_fixture fixture;
+static arena input, producer, detached, bridge_input;
+static pin_value call_result, bridge_plan;
+static compiler_prepared_scalar_declaration bridge_declaration;
+static uint64_t bridge_ready;
+static unsigned char *bridge_bytes;
+static size_t bridge_length;
+static int bridge_rejections;
+static behavior_run_counts bootstrap_counts;
+static behavior_function_context context;
+static behavior_function_activation activation;
+static service_binding *services;
+static compiler_prepared_fixture_service configuration;
+static node_host_call payload_call, syntax_call;
+static native_definition_binding payload_binding, syntax_binding;
+static compiler_host *host;
+static compiler_host_result target;
+static unsigned char *load_bytes;
+static int compile_calls, payload_calls, raw_parses, target_runs, offered_files;
+static char padded[SOURCE_CAP + 1], oversized[SOURCE_CAP + 2];
+static char long_path[PATH_CAP + 2], expression24[192], expression25[192];
+static const behavior_backend backends[] = { BEHAVIOR_BYTECODE, BEHAVIOR_SLJIT };
+
+static void cleanup_call()
+{
+    behavior_function_release_host(&context);
+    behavior_function_activation_free(&activation);
+    context = (behavior_function_context){ 0 };
+    activation = (behavior_function_activation){ 0 };
+    arena_free(&producer);
+    arena_free(&input);
+    arena_free(&detached);
+    afree(services);
+}
+static void cleanup()
+{
+    cleanup_call();
+    compiler_host_free(host);
+    host = NULL;
+    free(target.json);
+    target = (compiler_host_result){ 0 };
+    free(load_bytes);
+    load_bytes = NULL;
+    free(bridge_bytes);
+    bridge_bytes = NULL;
+    arena_free(&bridge_input);
+    bridge_plan = (pin_value){ 0 };
+    for (int b = 0; b < 2; b++) {
+        for (int i = 0; i < CASES; i++) {
+            free(outputs[b][i].bytes);
+            outputs[b][i] = (saved){ 0 };
+        }
+    }
+    compiler_fixture_free(&fixture);
+}
+static const char *observe_payload(
+    const behavior_function_context *ctx,
+    void *service,
+    const pin_value *arguments,
+    pin_value *results
+)
+{
+    payload_calls++;
+    if (!bridge_ready) {
+        if (pin_value_snapshot_to_arena(&bridge_input, &bridge_plan, &arguments[0])) {
+            return "Cannot retain bounded compiler plan for bridge rejection "
+                   "checks";
+        }
+        const compiler_prepared_fixture_service *config = service;
+        bridge_ready = config->ready_tag;
+        size_t bytes = strlen(arguments[3].str) + 1;
+        char *entry = arena_alloc(&bridge_input, bytes);
+        memcpy(entry, arguments[3].str, bytes);
+        bridge_declaration = (compiler_prepared_scalar_declaration){
+            .module = arguments[1].u64,
+            .function = arguments[2].u64,
+            .entry = entry,
+            .result = arguments[4].i
+        };
+    }
+    return COMPILER_PREPARED_FIXTURE_DEFINITION_PACK.bindings[0]
+        .implementation.call->context(ctx, service, arguments, results);
+}
+static const char *observe_syntax(
+    const behavior_function_context *ctx,
+    void *service,
+    const pin_value *arguments,
+    pin_value *results
+)
+{
+    raw_parses++;
+    if (arguments[0].type != PIN_STR || !arguments[0].str ||
+        strlen(arguments[0].str) > SOURCE_CAP) {
+        return "Bounded compiler passed oversized source to its raw parser";
+    }
+    return COMPILER_SYNTAX_DEFINITION_PACK.bindings[0]
+        .implementation.call->context(ctx, service, arguments, results);
+}
+static pin_value integer(int n)
+{
+    return (pin_value){ .type = PIN_I32, .i = n };
+}
+static pin_value text(const char *s)
+{
+    size_t bytes = strlen(s) + 1;
+    char *copy = arena_alloc(&input, bytes);
+    memcpy(copy, s, bytes);
+    return (pin_value){ .type = PIN_STR, .str = copy };
+}
+static bool put(pin_value *row, const char *name, pin_value value)
+{
+    const type_field *field = pin_type_field_path(pin_value_type(row), name);
+    REQUIRE(field && field->type == value.type);
+    pin_write_field(row->ptr, field, value);
+    return true;
+}
+static bool get(const pin_value *row, const char *name, pin_value *out)
+{
+    REQUIRE(row->type == PIN_STRUCT && row->ptr);
+    const type_field *field = pin_type_field_path(pin_value_type(row), name);
+    REQUIRE(field);
+    pin_read_field(row->ptr, field, out);
+    return true;
+}
+static uint64_t tag(int b, const char *package, const char *name, const char *variant)
+{
+    const authoring_package *owner = compiler_fixture_package(&fixture, b, package);
+    if (!owner || !owner->exports) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    const script_catalog_type *type = script_catalog_type_by_id(
+        owner->exports->metadata,
+        compiler_fixture_export(&fixture, b, package, name)
+    );
+    for (int i = 0; type && i < type->variant_count; i++) {
+        if (!strcmp(type->variants[i].name, variant)) {
+            return type->variants[i].tag;
+        }
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+static pin_value strings(const char *const *items, int count)
+{
+    pin_array *array = pin_array_snapshot_allocate(&input, PIN_STR, NULL, count);
+    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+        array->items[i] = text(items[i]);
+    }
+    return (pin_value){ .type = PIN_STR, .container = PIN_CONTAINER_ARRAY, .ptr = array };
+}
+static bool pack(int b, const request *r, pin_value *args)
+{
+    args[0] = text(r->project);
+    args[1] = strings(r->paths, r->path_count);
+    args[2] = strings(r->sources, r->source_count);
+    const pin_record *record = compiler_fixture_record(&fixture, b, "project:scalar_lowering", "Target", &input);
+    REQUIRE(record && record->type.field_count == 6);
+    args[3] = (pin_value){ .type = PIN_STRUCT,
+                           .ptr = arena_alloc(&input, record->type.size),
+                           .record = record,
+                           .type_name = record->type.name };
+    memset(args[3].ptr, 0, record->type.size);
+    const char *fields[] = { "schema",     "prepared",       "pointer_storage",
+                             "value_size", "payload_offset", "results_offset" };
+    int values[] = { 1,
+                     EXECUTION_PREPARED_VERSION,
+                     BF_POINTER_TYPE,
+                     sizeof(pin_value),
+                     offsetof(pin_value, d),
+                     offsetof(behavior_function_context, results) };
+    for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
+        REQUIRE(put(&args[3], fields[i], integer(values[i])));
+    }
+    if (r->wrong_abi) {
+        REQUIRE(put(&args[3], "prepared", integer(EXECUTION_PREPARED_VERSION + 1)));
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+static bool compile(int b, pin_value *args, pin_value *out)
+{
+    const authoring_package *package = compiler_fixture_package(&fixture, b, PACKAGE);
+    REQUIRE(package && package->valid && package->module);
+    uint64_t entry = compiler_fixture_export(&fixture, b, PACKAGE, "Compile");
+    REQUIRE(entry);
+    const script_catalog_capability
+        *signature = script_catalog_capability_by_id(package->exports->metadata, entry);
+    REQUIRE(signature && signature->result_count == 1);
+    const behavior_function *function = NULL;
+    for (int i = 0; i < execution_module_function_count(package->module); i++) {
+        execution_module_function_info
+            info = execution_module_function_at(package->module, i);
+        if (info.id == entry) {
+            function = info.body;
+        }
+    }
+    REQUIRE(function);
+    if (behavior_function_resumable(function)) {
+        behavior_function_activation_init(function, &activation);
+    }
+    call_result = (pin_value){ .type = signature->results[0].type.storage,
+                               .container = signature->results[0].type.container };
+    context = (behavior_function_context){
+        .activation = behavior_function_resumable(function) ? &activation : NULL,
+        .arguments = args,
+        .argument_count = 4,
+        .results = &call_result,
+        .budget = COMPILE_BUDGET
+    };
+    behavior_function_bind_storage(&context, &producer);
+    configuration.ready_tag = tag(b, "project:scalar_lowering", "Plan", "Ready");
+    REQUIRE(configuration.ready_tag);
+    apush(services, ((service_binding){ COMPILER_PREPARED_FIXTURE_SERVICE, &configuration }));
+    REQUIRE(behavior_function_bind(function, &context, services, 0));
+    behavior_run_scope runs = { 0 };
+    behavior_run_scope_begin(&runs);
+    compile_calls++;
+    int status = behavior_function_run(function, &context, b != 0);
+    behavior_run_scope_end(&runs);
+    if (status != FLOW_OK || !context.returned) {
+        fprintf(
+            stderr,
+            "bounded compiler: backend=%d status=%d returned=%d: %s\n",
+            b,
+            status,
+            context.returned,
+            context.error_message ? context.error_message : ""
+        );
+    }
+    REQUIRE(status == FLOW_OK && context.returned);
+    REQUIRE(!runs.counts.overflow && !runs.counts.inspection_bytecode_fallbacks);
+    REQUIRE(!runs.counts.wasm_entries);
+    REQUIRE(
+        b ? runs.counts.sljit_entries > 0 && !runs.counts.bytecode_entries
+          : runs.counts.bytecode_entries > 0 && !runs.counts.sljit_entries
+    );
+    REQUIRE(!pin_value_snapshot_to_arena(&detached, out, &call_result));
+    /* Deliberately retire arguments, activation and producer before examining
+     * detached output, including diagnostic text and each byte element. */
+    behavior_function_release_host(&context);
+    behavior_function_activation_free(&activation);
+    context = (behavior_function_context){ 0 };
+    activation = (behavior_function_activation){ 0 };
+    arena_free(&producer);
+    arena_free(&input);
+    afree(services);
+    return true;
+}
+static uint64_t little_endian(const unsigned char *bytes)
+{
+    uint64_t value = 0;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
+        value |= (uint64_t)bytes[i] << (8 * i);
+    }
+    return value;
+}
+static bool retain(int b, int index, const pin_value *result)
+{
+    saved *out = &outputs[b][index];
+    REQUIRE(result->type == PIN_UNION && result->ptr);
+    const pin_union *value = result->ptr;
+    if (index >= ACCEPTED) {
+        REQUIRE(value->tag == tag(b, PACKAGE, "Result", "Rejected") && value->count == 1);
+        const char *fields[] = { "start", "end", "line", "column", "document" };
+        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
+            pin_value field;
+            REQUIRE(get(&value->values[0], fields[i], &field) && field.type == PIN_I32);
+            out->location[i] = field.i;
+        }
+        pin_value diagnostic;
+        REQUIRE(get(&value->values[0], "message", &diagnostic));
+        REQUIRE(diagnostic.type == PIN_STR && diagnostic.str && diagnostic.str[0]);
+        REQUIRE(strlen(diagnostic.str) < sizeof out->diagnostic);
+        memcpy(out->diagnostic, diagnostic.str, strlen(diagnostic.str) + 1);
+        return true;
+    }
+    REQUIRE(value->tag == tag(b, PACKAGE, "Result", "Compiled") && value->count == 3);
+    REQUIRE(value->values[0].type == PIN_U64 && value->values[0].u64);
+    REQUIRE(value->values[1].type == PIN_U64 && value->values[1].u64);
+    out->module = value->values[0].u64;
+    out->entry = value->values[1].u64;
+    REQUIRE(out->module == script_catalog_id("module", "project:facts"));
+    REQUIRE(out->entry == script_catalog_id("package-symbol", "project:facts:1:Answer:callable"));
+    const pin_value *bytes = &value->values[2];
+    REQUIRE(
+        bytes->type == PIN_U8 && bytes->container == PIN_CONTAINER_ARRAY &&
+        bytes->ptr
+    );
+    const pin_array *array = bytes->ptr;
+    REQUIRE(array->count > 56 && array->count <= ARTIFACT_CAP);
+    out->length = (size_t)array->count;
+    out->bytes = xmalloc(out->length);
+    for (int i = 0; i < array->count; i++) {
+        REQUIRE(array->items[i].type == PIN_U8 && array->items[i].container == PIN_CONTAINER_SINGLE);
+        out->bytes[i] = array->items[i].u8;
+    }
+    REQUIRE(!memcmp(out->bytes, "CHIBICLO", 8));
+    REQUIRE(little_endian(out->bytes + 8) == 1);
+    REQUIRE(little_endian(out->bytes + 16) == out->module);
+    REQUIRE(little_endian(out->bytes + 24) == 1);
+    REQUIRE(little_endian(out->bytes + 32) == out->module);
+    size_t name_length = (size_t)little_endian(out->bytes + 40);
+    size_t payload_length = (size_t)little_endian(out->bytes + 48);
+    REQUIRE(name_length == strlen("project:facts"));
+    REQUIRE(payload_length > 0 && 56 + name_length <= out->length);
+    REQUIRE(payload_length == out->length - 56 - name_length);
+    REQUIRE(!memcmp(out->bytes + 56, "project:facts", name_length));
+    return true;
+}
+static bool same_artifact(const saved *a, const saved *b)
+{
+    REQUIRE(a->module == b->module && a->entry == b->entry);
+    REQUIRE(a->length == b->length && a->length > 0);
+    REQUIRE(!memcmp(a->bytes, b->bytes, a->length));
+    return true;
+}
+static bool run_target(int producer_backend, int index, int target_backend)
+{
+    const saved *artifact = &outputs[producer_backend][index];
+    load_bytes = xmalloc(artifact->length);
+    memcpy(load_bytes, artifact->bytes, artifact->length);
+    char error[256];
+    host = compiler_host_load(load_bytes, artifact->length, backends[target_backend], error, sizeof error);
+    free(load_bytes);
+    load_bytes = NULL; /* Load must own all data before the offered bytes retire. */
+    if (!host) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "bounded artifact load: %s\n", error);
+    }
+    REQUIRE(host);
+    target_runs++;
+    bool valid = compiler_host_invoke(host, artifact->entry, "[]", 2, TARGET_BUDGET, &target);
+    compiler_host_free(host);
+    host = NULL; /* Result JSON must outlive the consuming runtime as well. */
+    if (!valid) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "bounded artifact run: %s\n", target.diagnostic);
+    }
+    REQUIRE(valid && target.flow_status == FLOW_OK);
+    REQUIRE(!target.counts.overflow && !target.counts.inspection_bytecode_fallbacks);
+    REQUIRE(!target.counts.wasm_entries);
+    REQUIRE(
+        target_backend
+            ? target.counts.sljit_entries == 1 && !target.counts.bytecode_entries
+            : target.counts.bytecode_entries == 1 && !target.counts.sljit_entries
+    );
+    REQUIRE(target.json && target.length == strlen(cases[index].expected));
+    REQUIRE(!strcmp(target.json, cases[index].expected));
+    free(target.json);
+    target = (compiler_host_result){ 0 };
+    return true;
+}
